# Structured flow (GAME-05/06): end-of-phase pass rounds with auto-pass, actions, block windows.
# Seating A B C: A's prey is B, its predator C.
seed 5
seat A alice
seat B bob
seat C carol
crypt A "Vera Nightfall" *12
library A "Iron Ward" *40
crypt B "Tomas Grey" *12
library B "Quick Feed" *40
crypt C "Ilse Várga" *12
library C "Signal Fire" *40
start

A> transfer +4 A:uncontrolled:1
A> move A:uncontrolled:1 ready
B> transfer +4 B:uncontrolled:1
B> move B:uncontrolled:1 ready
C> transfer +4 C:uncontrolled:1
C> move C:uncontrolled:1 ready

# Everyone auto-passes by default, so phases advance at once.
expect autopass B unlock,master,minion,influence,discard
A> next
expect turn 1 A master
expect window none
expect waiting A:phase

# B wants a say at every phase end now.
B> autopass none
expect autopass B none
A> next
expect window phase master
expect impulse B
expect waiting B:impulse
log public End of A's master phase: waiting for the other players
reject:not-now A> next
reject:not-now C> pass
reject:forbidden C> next
# A play during the round returns the impulse to the acting Methuselah, and is replaced.
B> play "Quick Feed"
expect impulse A
expect count B:hand 7
expect count B:ashHeap 1
log public B played Quick Feed
A> pass
expect impulse B
B> pass
expect window none
expect turn 1 A minion

# A bleed: the prey may block; C, not eligible, passes automatically.
reject:forbidden B> bleed B:ready:1
A> bleed A:ready:1
expect action bleed A blocks
expect card A:ready:1 locked true
expect impulse B
expect waiting B:block
log public A: Vera Nightfall bleeds B
reject:not-now C> block C:ready:1
reject:not-now A> next
reject:not-now A> resolve success
B> pass
log public B declined to block
expect action bleed A resolution
# Not blocked: the would-be-successful window opens, A first, for cards played "if the bleed would
# be successful" (zero-vtes digest §10.1). Resolving would pass it, but B passes nothing
# automatically: A passes, then B, and A resolves.
expect window would-succeed minion
expect waiting A:resolve
reject:forbidden B> resolve success
reject:not-now A> resolve success 2 edge
A> pass
expect impulse B
B> pass
expect window none
A> resolve success 2 edge
expect pool B 24
expect edge A
log public The action succeeded
# Then its after-resolution window, A first (§10.4): the next action or the end of the phase would
# pass it, but B is still to pass by hand.
expect window after-resolution minion
reject:not-now A> next
A> pass
B> pass
expect action none

# Locked minions can't act.
reject:invalid A> hunt A:ready:1
A> unlock A:ready:1

# A hunt, undirected: prey and predator may block. B tries, A answers, B gives up.
A> hunt A:ready:1
expect impulse B
B> block B:ready:1
log public B tries to block with Tomas Grey
expect impulse A
# With a block attempt pending, A only has the impulse.
expect waiting A:impulse
reject:not-now B> play B:hand:1
A> play A:hand:1
expect impulse A
expect count A:hand 7
A> pass
expect impulse B
B> unblock
log public B withdrew the block
expect impulse C
C> pass
log public C declined to block
expect action hunt A resolution
A> resolve success 5
expect card A:ready:1 blood 7
expect card B:ready:1 locked false
A> pass
B> pass

# Equip, blocked by B: the blocker locks, and the card goes to the ash heap after combat.
A> unlock A:ready:1
A> equip A:ready:1 with A:hand:1
log public A: Vera Nightfall equips with Iron Ward
B> block B:ready:1
A> pass
B> pass
C> pass
expect action equip A combat
expect waiting A:combat
expect card B:ready:1 locked true
log public Tomas Grey blocks: combat
reject:forbidden C> endcombat
B> endcombat
# Ending it early still leaves the end of the round (zero-vtes rules-qa 19.5).
A> pass
B> pass
# B ended combat, but the card and its replacement are A's.
log public A played Iron Ward
log public A drew 1 card from their library
A> pass
B> pass
expect action none
expect count A:ashHeap 2
expect count A:hand 7

# A successful equip attaches the card.
A> unlock A:ready:1
A> equip A:ready:1 with A:hand:1
B> pass
C> pass
A> resolve success
expect card A:ready:2 attached Vera Nightfall
expect count A:hand 7
A> pass
B> pass

# Cancelling an action (an override) closes its window.
A> unlock A:ready:1
A> action A:ready:1
A> cancel
expect action none
expect window none
log public A cancelled the action

# B stops the round, then switches auto-pass back on while holding the impulse.
A> next
expect impulse B
B> autopass all
expect window none
expect turn 1 A influence
A> next
A> next
# The new turn starts by unlocking the new Methuselah's cards.
expect turn 2 B unlock
expect card B:ready:1 locked false
expect card A:ready:1 locked true
